NAME
     mv - move or rename files

SYNOPSIS
     mv SOURCE... TARGET

DESCRIPTION
     With one SOURCE and a TARGET that is not a directory, mv renames
     SOURCE to TARGET. Otherwise TARGET must be a directory and each
     SOURCE is moved into it under its own name. A rename within one file
     system moves no data; across file systems mv copies and unlinks.

SEE ALSO
     cp(1), ln(1), rm(1)
